  "rationale": "In vivo validation pool: 196 guides on 98 SDL candidate genes (2 per gene), no non-targeting guides in the deposited table, tumors grown in 7 models with 'Wild Type' and 'cas9' arms in duplicate. Column names match GSM titles. HT1080 = HTelo- (hTERT-low), HT_TERT = HTelo+ (GFP-hTERT). The paper's Fig. 2d compares HTelo+ with HTelo- tumors; the primary analysis is HTelo+ cas9 vs HTelo- cas9 (2 vs 2). If 'Wild Type' means no Cas9, the cleaner SDL contrast is the line x Cas9 interaction (8 tumors), kept as the second analysis; Cas9 vs Wild Type within HTelo+ and within each of the five other models mirrors the paper's per-model MAGeCK plots (Fig. 2e). GEO does not say that Wild Type tumors lack Cas9, so the Cas9 vs WT contrasts are interpretable only under that assumption. Library totals; no controls, so calibration cannot be checked. HTelo+ vs HTelo- within the Wild Type arm is run as a check: if Wild Type tumors lack Cas9, no gene should differ there."
